      "id": 1,
      "text": "Charles City County was one of Virginia’s eight original shires, formed in 1634 and named after Charles City at Bermuda Hundred.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Charles-City-county-Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The county hosts some of Virginia’s oldest plantations, including Berkeley, Westover, Greenway, and Shirley, all National Historic Landmarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Charles-City-county-Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Bowman Center for Local History, a reference library and archives, sits in the Charles City County Library Building.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
